# Generated by Next.js, and its contents depend on whether `next dev` or `next build` ran last —
# which makes it output, not source. Tracking it meant every production build (and therefore every
# e2e run, since the suite now builds) left `git status` dirty, and PROCESS.md's "a test suite never
# writes into the working tree" rule was paid for with a defect that survived two reviews.
# turbo.json makes `typecheck` depend on `build` so the file exists before anything reads it.
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
